| blue-soft | #EEF2FF | accepted/solved backgrounds |

Logo: use `/community-logo.png` on light backgrounds and `/community-logo-reversed.png` on dark. Header is light/glass, not dark. Tagline: Ask · Share · Ride.
Never use red/green alone to mean state; status is blue/green plus a text label.

## Type
- Display/headings: Archivo, `font-stretch: 75%`, weight 800, UPPERCASE, tight line-height (0.95–1.05). H1 56–76px, section H2 22–44px.
- Body: IBM Plex Sans 15–17px, line-height 1.5–1.65.
- Data (prices, Spokes, years, serials, tags, eyebrows): IBM Plex Mono. Eyebrows are 12–13px, letter-spacing 0.12em, uppercase.

## Shape & spacing
- Radius: cards 14–16px, buttons/inputs 8–10px, chips/pills 999px, thumbnails 8px.
- Card: white, 1px `line` border, padding 20–24px, no heavy shadows.
- Page container: max-width 1280px, 32px side padding. Layouts: content column + sidebar using `flex-wrap`; sidebar stacks below on mobile.
- Touch targets ≥ 44px tall.

## Shared components (build once, reuse)
- `SiteHeader` — dark bar: logo, nav (Community, Garages, Experts, Resources, Market), search, "Ask the community" button, avatar
- `Avatar` — initials fallback on a colored circle; photo when present
- `RatingStars` — star icon + number + "(n reviews)"
- `SpokesCount` — mono number + "Spokes"; `LevelBadge` (RIDER / PRO / MASTER / LEGEND, mono, ink bg)
- `ExpertiseBadge` — "Verified · {area}" ink pill
- `StatusChip` — For sale (accent bg), Open to offers (blue bg), Trade only (outlined ink), Not for sale (outlined grey)
- `PersonRow`, `QuestionCard`, `AnswerCard`, `GarageCard`, `ItemCard`, `ValueRange`, `ValueTrendBars`, `ContributionCalendar`, `TagChip`, `FilterChip`, `SegmentedControl`

## Accessibility
Real `<button>`, `<a>`, `<label>` + inputs; `aria-label` on icon-only buttons; decorative SVG `aria-hidden`; 4.5:1 text contrast; visible focus rings.

## Conventions
- Icons: lucide-react, 1.5–2.2 stroke. No emoji in UI.
- Never invent production numbers; read from the database. Seed data may reuse the mockup sample data.
- Market values are always shown as a range plus "estimate" disclaimer.
